module {input: "each", defaults: {threshold: 0.5}};
# same-page: the screenshots that still look like a known-good one
#
#   deem run --img baseline screens/orders.png same-page screens/orders*.png
#
# A visual check after a deploy: `.` is each new screenshot, and
# `--img baseline FILE` makes $baseline a screenshot of the same page from
# when it looked right. Only the screenshots that still look like it print.
# The orders page with its stylesheet missing has the same text, and isn't
# the same page to a user, so the question asks how it looks, not what it
# says. Both pictures go in one value, and the question names each part in
# backticks, as the API's docs recommend. Each screenshot is a request with
# both pictures in it, and every screenshot's request goes out in the same
# wave.

def main:
  "does `screen` look like `baseline`, with the same layout and styling?" as $q
  | select(ask($q; {screen: ., baseline: $baseline}) > $threshold);
